# Ark UI documentation (LLMs.txt)

Webmail uses **@ark-ui/svelte** (Svelte 5). Prefer Ark UI APIs over Radix/shadcn assumptions.

Official guide: [Ark UI LLMs.txt](https://ark-ui.com/docs/ai/llms.txt)

## LLMs.txt routes

| Route | URL | When to use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Index (all frameworks) | https://ark-ui.com/llms.txt | Overview / cross-framework links |
| **Svelte** (primary) | https://ark-ui.com/llms-svelte.txt | Default for webmail |
| Full documentation | https://ark-ui.com/llms-full.txt | Deep dive on unfamiliar primitives |

## Workflow

Before implementing or changing `@ark-ui/svelte/*` imports:

1. Fetch **llms-svelte.txt** (or follow links from that index for the specific component).
2. Match APIs to the installed `@ark-ui/svelte` version in `apps/webmail/package.json`.
3. Check the local inventory: `apps/webmail/docs/ark-ui-components.md`.
4. Reuse existing wrappers in `apps/webmail/src/lib/components/ui/` when present.

Do not quote entire upstream pages; cite component names or doc paths only.

## Cursor @Docs

In **Settings → Features → Docs**, add:

- `https://ark-ui.com/llms-svelte.txt`

Reference with `@Docs` in chat when working on Ark UI components.
